      "en": "An **array** is an ordered list of values in `[ ]`: `const cities = [\"Cairo\", \"Giza\", \"Alex\"];`. The first item has index **0**: `cities[0]`, and the last is `cities.at(-1)`. `cities.length` is the number of items. You can store any type, even mixed ones, but in real work keep one type (all numbers, or all order objects)."
