      "en": "`arr[i] = value` changes the item at that position. Writing to a far index (`arr[10] = x` on an array of 3) creates «empty slots» — avoid it. `length` updates by itself. To empty an array: `arr.length = 0` (it empties the same array for everyone pointing at it)."
