      "en": "`[10, 9, 100].sort()` gives `[10, 100, 9]`! Because sort with no function sorts **as text**. Numbers need a compare function: `sort((a, b) => a - b)` ascending and `(a, b) => b - a` descending. The function returns a negative number if a comes first, a positive one if after, and zero if equal. And remember sort changes the original — use toSorted or copy first."
